The colours, which the sample editor shares.


METHOD:: bpmDialog
ARGUMENT:: sdg
the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.
ARGUMENT:: pairs
code::[[path, seconds] ...]::: the files, and how long each is.
ARGUMENT:: bankName
for the title, when the files are a bank's.
ARGUMENT:: where
a link::Classes/Point::, the dialog's top left.
A small window to set a bpm by hand. A bpm typed goes to every file; beats typed instead give each
file the bpm its own length makes of them. ÷2 and ×2 act on the box; strong::back to the analysis::
forgets what was set by hand. Return keeps, escape leaves. One at a time.
RETURNS:: the Window.

METHOD:: bpmDialogWindow
RETURNS:: the bpm dialog, open or last closed.

METHOD:: panelWidth
The right panel's width in a new window, pixels: the last width it was dragged to. 450 to start.

METHOD:: minPanelWidth
The narrowest the right panel goes, 360.

METHOD:: explorerColumnKeys
The columns of a new window.

METHOD:: explorerColumnSpecs
Every column there is, an Event each: code::key::, code::label::, and
code::width:: and code::align:: for the fixed ones.

METHOD:: parseSearch
ARGUMENT:: str
what is in the search field.
RETURNS:: an Event: code::words::, code::include:: and code::exclude:: (tags),
code::bpm::, code::key:: (from link::Classes/SDGSampleFeatures#*parseKey::).

METHOD:: durationRange
ARGUMENT:: durs
a bank's durations, seconds.
RETURNS:: the shortest to the longest, code::"0.12-3.4"::, as the explorer shows a bank; one number when they are all the same.

METHOD:: dateString
ARGUMENT:: seconds
seconds since 1970, UTC.
RETURNS:: code::"2025-08-25"::, or an empty String for nil.

METHOD:: naturalKey
METHOD:: foldBpm
METHOD:: keyOrder
What the name, bpm and key columns sort by.

METHOD:: notesColumns
How many characters fit across the modules tab's notes, where a parameter's description
wraps. 68 at the window's width.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: setPanelWidth
ARGUMENT:: w
The right panel this wide, pixels, kept between link::#*minPanelWidth:: and what leaves one strip
beside it; new windows open with it. What dragging the handle between the strips and the panel does.

METHOD:: panelHandle
RETURNS:: the handle between the strips and the right panel, a UserView.

METHOD:: sdg
METHOD:: dirt
The loader, and its SuperDirt.

METHOD:: window
The link::Classes/Window::.

METHOD:: isOpen
METHOD:: front
METHOD:: close
The window's state. Closing stops the meters and the library poll and takes
the window off the loader's dependants.

METHOD:: selectOrbit
METHOD:: selectedOrbitIndex
METHOD:: selectedOrbit
The orbit the effects tab shows and the explorer plays into.

METHOD:: selectTab
METHOD:: tab
METHOD:: walkTabs
The tab on the right: 0 effects, 1 sound explorer, 2 modules.

METHOD:: refreshMixer
Put the faders, mutes and solos to the loader's state. Called on its
code::\mixer:: notification.

METHOD:: addInsert
What + insert and the effects tab's add do: link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-addInsert::,
and the new insert's window opened - for code::\vst::, link::#-vstDialog:: first.
ARGUMENT:: i
the orbit's index.
ARGUMENT:: kind
code::\eq::, code::\compressor::, code::\insight:: or code::\vst::.
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/SDGInsert::, or nil - always nil for code::\vst::,
whose insert is made once a plugin is picked.

METHOD:: vstDialog
The window + insert's VST plugin... opens: the VST effects the server can open
(link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-vstPlugins::), a search over their names and
vendors, and rescan. Insert, enter or a double click puts the chosen one on the
orbit and shows its editor once it has loaded.
ARGUMENT:: i
the orbit's index.
RETURNS:: the dialog's link::Classes/Window::.

METHOD:: rebuildStripInserts
METHOD:: rebuildInsertRows
Read an orbit's inserts again: a strip's buttons, and the effects tab's rows
for the selected orbit. Called on the loader's code::\inserts:: notification.

METHOD:: peakHolds
Per orbit, the highest peak since its readout was last clicked, as an
amplitude.

METHOD:: trackViews
RETURNS:: an Event of views per strip on show: code::track::, code::label::, code::loadMenu::, code::candidates::, code::meters::, code::fader::, code::faderText::.

METHOD:: rebuildTrackStrips
Make the selected orbit's strips again, and send meter numbers only for them.

METHOD:: refreshTrackLevels
The strips' faders to their tracks' levels.

METHOD:: loadTrackEffect
What a strip's menu does: link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-setTrackEffect::, and the new effect's parameters shown.
ARGUMENT:: track
an link::Classes/SDGTrack::.
ARGUMENT:: name
the effect's name.
RETURNS:: the new link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect::, or nil.

METHOD:: rebuildEffectSection
Read the selected orbit's effects again.

METHOD:: addEffect
METHOD:: removeEffect
METHOD:: moveEffect
What the effect rows do, from code.

METHOD:: search
The explorer's search string.

METHOD:: loadFolder
What the load folder... buttons do once a folder is picked:
link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-loadSamples::, then the search cleared and the first
new bank selected. A folder with nothing new says so on the line under the tree.
ARGUMENT:: path
the folder, a String.
RETURNS:: the names of the banks that got files.

METHOD:: loadFolderDialog
The folder dialog in front of link::#-loadFolder::.

METHOD:: refreshExplorer
Build the list from the sound library again, searched and sorted; what was
selected is selected again if it is still there, and the banks that were open
stay open.

METHOD:: explorerModel
What the list shows, one Event per bank in the order shown:
code::(kind: \bank, name:, files:, fileData:, numBuffers:):: - code::files:: the
indices of its samples in the order shown, code::fileData:: an Event per sample
with its Buffer and its link::Classes/SDGSampleTags#-infoOf:: - and
code::(kind: \synths, names:):: last.

METHOD:: sortBy
Sort the explorer by a column, as a click on its header does.
ARGUMENT:: key
code::\name::, code::\duration::, code::\number::, code::\bpm::, code::\key::,
code::\tags::, code::\added:: or code::\created::. The bpm sorts folded into
80 .. 160, so a loop at 70 sits by one at 140; with code::bpm:: in the search, by
how close it is, halves and doubles counted.
ARGUMENT:: ascending
nil: ascending on the first click (newest first for the dates), the other way
on the next.

METHOD:: sortKey
METHOD:: sortAscending
What the explorer is sorted by. A session keeps both.

METHOD:: explorerColumns
The columns on show, code::\name:: first; a session keeps them.
code::
~sdg.gui.explorerColumns = [\name, \duration, \number, \bpm, \added];
::

METHOD:: toggleSearchTag
Put code::tag:x:: in the search, or take it out - what a tag button does.
ARGUMENT:: tag
the tag.
ARGUMENT:: exclude
true for code::-tag:x::.

METHOD:: openAll
METHOD:: closeAll
METHOD:: toggleBank
METHOD:: expandBank
METHOD:: isExpanded
Which banks are open. A bank opened goes first in the analysis queue. While
the search holds something, every bank is open until closed.

METHOD:: selectSound
Select a bank, or a sample of it (the bank opened), as a click would.
ARGUMENT:: name
the bank.
ARGUMENT:: index
the sample, or nil for the bank.

METHOD:: selectedPaths
The files the selection stands for: the sample's, or every one of a bank's.

METHOD:: addSelectedToSync
The selected sample, or every sample of a selected bank, into link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-sync::,
and its window opened - what code::y:: and strong::add to sync:: do.
RETURNS:: false when nothing that can be added is selected.

METHOD:: editBpmDialog
The bpm dialog (link::#*bpmDialog::) for the selected sample, or every sample of a selected bank -
what code::b:: and strong::set bpm...:: do.

METHOD:: editTagsDialog
A sample's tags as one line to change; on a bank, tags to add to every sample
of it, code::-x:: taking one away.

METHOD:: reanalyseAll
Analyse every sample with no fresh analysis.

METHOD:: selected
What is selected, as an Event with code::kind:: (code::\bank::, code::\sample::,
code::\synth::), code::name:: and code::index::, or nil.

METHOD:: selectedBuffer
The Buffer the selection stands for, the code::n:: box picking the sample.

METHOD:: playSelected
METHOD:: editSelected
METHOD:: revealSelected
The explorer's buttons, from code.

METHOD:: refreshLoaded
Put the modules tab's lists to the loader's names, each list keeping its
selection. Called on its code::\loaded:: notification.

METHOD:: loadedEntries
What the modules tab's lists show: an IdentityDictionary from kind to
link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-entries::.

METHOD:: notesString
What the bottom of the modules tab says about the selected name, as a String;
empty when nothing is selected.

METHOD:: editFile
Open the file a name came from, as edit... does.
ARGUMENT:: kind
code::\synths::, code::\modules::, code::\players:: or code::\effects::.
ARGUMENT:: name
the name; the one selected in that kind's list when nil.

METHOD:: newFileDialog
The window new... opens: a name, the file to copy, cancel and make.
ARGUMENT:: kind
code::\synths::, code::\modules::, code::\players:: or code::\effects::.
ARGUMENT:: from
the name whose file to copy; the one selected in the list, else the example,
when nil.
RETURNS:: the dialog's link::Classes/Window::.

METHOD:: makeFile
What make in that dialog does: link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-newFile::, then the
new name selected in its list and its file opened through link::#*openCode::.
code::
~sdg.gui.makeFile(\players, \mywarp);
::
ARGUMENT:: kind
code::\synths::, code::\modules::, code::\players:: or code::\effects::.
ARGUMENT:: name
the new name.
ARGUMENT:: from
the name whose file to copy; the example when nil.
RETURNS:: the path of the new file, or nil.
